   "line": [
    "Bb7"
   ],
   "spoken": "The bishop to b7, fianchettoed."
  },
  {
   "ply": 9,
   "t": 91,
   "fen": "rn1qkbnr/1b1ppppp/p7/1pp5/4P3/P1N3P1/1PPP1PBP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 2 5",
   "line": [
    "Bg2"
   ],
   "spoken": "Now a setup taught long ago: the pawns to d6 and e6, a Scheveningen-like structure controlling key central squares — passive-looking, but the heart of the Sicilian. You can start with the knight to f6, unafraid of e5 since the bishop on g2 would hang."
  },
  {
   "ply": 10,
   "t": 144.5,
   "fen": "rn1qkbnr/1b2pppp/p2p4/1pp5/4P3/P1N3P1/1PPP1PBP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "d6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Start with d6 — flexible, and it opens a future home on d7 for the other knight."
  },
  {
   "ply": 11,
   "t": 158,
   "fen": "rn1qkbnr/1b2pppp/p2p4/1pp5/4P3/P1NP2P1/1PP2PBP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 0 6",
   "line": [
    "d3"
   ],
   "spoken": "The knight often goes to d7 rather than c6, since c6 would block the bishop awkwardly."
  },
  {
   "ply": 12,
   "t": 168.5,
   "fen": "rn1qkbnr/1b3ppp/p2pp3/1pp5/4P3/P1NP2P1/1PP2PBP/R1BQK1NR w KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "e6"
   ],
   "spoken": "Then e6 — you can see why the pawns sit on d6 and e6: they control the centre and give the kingside pieces room."
  },
  {
   "ply": 13,
   "t": 180.5,
   "fen": "rn1qkbnr/1b3ppp/p2pp3/1pp5/4PP2/P1NP2P1/1PP3BP/R1BQK1NR b KQkq - 0 7",
   "line": [
    "f4"
